01:29:23.190 --> 01:29:25.230
And this is a,

01:29:25.230 --> 01:29:29.220
of course is a segue into
this incredible landscape,

01:29:29.220 --> 01:29:31.110
which is the gut brain axis,

01:29:31.110 --> 01:29:35.550
which I think 15 years ago was almost a,

01:29:35.550 --> 01:29:38.523
maybe it was posters at a meeting.

01:29:39.498 --> 01:29:41.913
And then now I believe you and others,

01:29:42.754 --> 01:29:44.160
there are companies, there have companies,

01:29:44.160 --> 01:29:47.580
there are active research programs,

01:29:47.580 --> 01:29:49.470
and beautiful work.

01:29:49.470 --> 01:29:50.850
Maybe you could describe some of that work

01:29:50.850 --> 01:29:52.800
that you and others have been involved in.

01:29:52.800 --> 01:29:57.240
And a lot of the listeners of
this podcast will have heard

01:29:57.240 --> 01:29:58.380
of the gut brain axis.

01:29:58.380 --> 01:30:00.630
And there are a lot of misconceptions

01:30:00.630 --> 01:30:01.620
about the gut brain axis.

01:30:01.620 --> 01:30:04.260
Many people think that this
means that we think with our

01:30:04.260 --> 01:30:09.260
stomach because of the quote
unquote, gut feeling aspect,

01:30:09.702 --> 01:30:12.240
but I'd love for you to talk
about the aspects of gut brain

01:30:12.240 --> 01:30:15.120
signaling that drive or
change our perceptions

01:30:15.120 --> 01:30:18.300
and behaviors that are
completely beneath our awareness.

01:30:18.300 --> 01:30:19.830
- Yes. Excellent.

01:30:19.830 --> 01:30:24.830
So let me begin maybe by stating that,

01:30:25.770 --> 01:30:29.320
the brain needs to monitor

01:30:30.660 --> 01:30:34.590
the state of every one of our organs,

01:30:34.590 --> 01:30:36.000
it has to do it.

01:30:36.000 --> 01:30:41.000
This is the only way that the
brain can ensure that every

01:30:41.040 --> 01:30:45.630
one of those organs are working
together in a way that we

01:30:45.630 --> 01:30:47.343
have healthy physiology.

01:30:49.380 --> 01:30:50.670
Now,

01:30:50.670 --> 01:30:55.380
this monitoring of the brain
has been known for a long time,

01:30:55.380 --> 01:30:58.260
but I think what hadn't been
fully appreciated that this is

01:30:58.260 --> 01:31:03.093
a two-way highway where the
brain is not only monitoring,

01:31:04.140 --> 01:31:09.140
but is now modulating back
what the body needs to do.

01:31:11.437 --> 01:31:14.550
And that includes all the way
from monitoring the frequency

01:31:14.550 --> 01:31:19.550
of heartbeats and the way that
inspiration and aspirations

01:31:19.620 --> 01:31:23.640
in the breeding cycle operate
to what happens when you

01:31:23.640 --> 01:31:25.623
ingest sugar and fat.

01:31:28.320 --> 01:31:32.973
Now, let me give you an example again,

01:31:36.821 --> 01:31:38.137
of how the brain can take

01:31:41.070 --> 01:31:46.070
what we would refer to contextual
associations and transform

01:31:46.770 --> 01:31:51.063
it into incredible changes
in physiology and metabolism.

01:31:52.950 --> 01:31:55.013
Remember Pavlov?

01:31:55.013 --> 01:31:58.350
So Pavlov in his classical
experiments in conditioning,

01:31:58.350 --> 01:32:02.370
associative conditioning,
he would take a bell,

01:32:02.370 --> 01:32:04.630
he would ring the bell every time

01:32:05.595 --> 01:32:06.743
he was going to feed the dog.

01:32:08.383 --> 01:32:10.800
And eventually the dog
learned to associate

01:32:10.800 --> 01:32:14.467
the ringing of the bell with food coming.

01:32:14.467 --> 01:32:18.330
Now, the first incredible finding

01:32:18.330 --> 01:32:21.900
he made is the fact that the dog now

01:32:21.900 --> 01:32:24.480
in the presence of the bell alone

01:32:24.480 --> 01:32:25.953
will start to salivate.

01:32:27.180 --> 01:32:28.770
And we will call that

01:32:28.770 --> 01:32:32.943
neurologically speaking
an anticipatory response.

01:32:34.140 --> 01:32:35.640
Okay, I could understand it.

01:32:35.640 --> 01:32:36.930
I get it.

01:32:36.930 --> 01:32:39.000
You know, neurons in the brain that form

01:32:39.000 --> 01:32:42.900
that association now
represent food is coming.

01:32:42.900 --> 01:32:47.700
And they're sending a signal
to motor neurons to go into

01:32:47.700 --> 01:32:50.070
your salivary glands to squeeze them.

01:32:50.070 --> 01:32:55.070
So you release saliva because
you know food is coming,

01:32:56.010 --> 01:32:59.490
but what's even more remarkable
is that those animals are

01:32:59.490 --> 01:33:04.490
also releasing insulin
in response to a bell.

01:33:06.240 --> 01:33:07.073
Okay.

01:33:09.474 --> 01:33:13.080
This illustrates one part
of this two-way highway,

01:33:13.080 --> 01:33:14.793
the highway going down,

01:33:15.780 --> 01:33:18.630
somehow the brain created these
associations and there are

01:33:18.630 --> 01:33:23.220
neurons in your brain now that
no food is coming and send a

01:33:23.220 --> 01:33:28.062
signal somehow all the way down
to your pancreas that now it

01:33:28.062 --> 01:33:31.623
says release insulin because
sugar is coming down.

01:33:33.294 --> 01:33:36.227
This goes back to the magic of the brain.

01:33:36.227 --> 01:33:40.350
It's a never ending source
of both joy and intrigue.

01:33:40.350 --> 01:33:42.063
How the hell do they do this?

01:33:43.230 --> 01:33:45.003
I mean, the neurons.

01:33:45.003 --> 01:33:47.850
- I share your delight and fascination.

01:33:47.850 --> 01:33:52.850
There's not a day or a lecture
or some talks are better than

01:33:53.760 --> 01:33:56.410
others or talk where I don't
sit back and just think,

01:33:57.398 --> 01:33:58.964
it's absolutely amazing.

01:33:58.964 --> 01:34:00.520
- How.
- It's amazing.

01:34:00.520 --> 01:34:02.790
- Now over the past, I don't know,

01:34:02.790 --> 01:34:06.222
dozen years it and with great force

01:34:06.222 --> 01:34:07.960
over the last five years

01:34:09.780 --> 01:34:12.900
now, the main highway
that is communicating

01:34:12.900 --> 01:34:15.663
the state of the body with the brain,

01:34:17.304 --> 01:34:19.863
it has been uncovered as being

01:34:19.863 --> 01:34:23.730
what we now refer to
as the gut brain axis.

01:34:23.730 --> 01:34:27.730
And the highway is a
specific bundle of nerves

01:34:29.400 --> 01:34:33.030
which emerged from the Vagal
ganglia, the nodus ganglia.

01:34:33.030 --> 01:34:37.710
And so it's the vagus
nerve that is innervating

01:34:37.710 --> 01:34:40.983
the majority of the organs in your body.

01:34:42.120 --> 01:34:44.550
It's monitoring their function,

01:34:44.550 --> 01:34:46.890
sending a signal to the brain.

01:34:46.890 --> 01:34:50.400
And now the brain going
back down and saying,

01:34:50.400 --> 01:34:52.230
this is going alright, do this,

01:34:52.230 --> 01:34:54.483
or this is not going too well, do that.

01:34:55.500 --> 01:34:58.590
- And I should point out as
you well know, every organ,

01:34:58.590 --> 01:35:01.680
spleen, pancreas, lung.

01:35:01.680 --> 01:35:03.693
- They all must be monitored.

01:35:04.920 --> 01:35:06.813
In fact I now,

01:35:08.389 --> 01:35:11.670
I have no doubt that the
diseases that we have normally

01:35:11.670 --> 01:35:15.153
associated with metabolism, physiology,

01:35:16.193 --> 01:35:21.193
and even immunity are likely
to emerge as diseases,

01:35:23.220 --> 01:35:25.983
conditions, states of the brain.

01:35:27.450 --> 01:35:30.513
I don't think obesity is
a disease of metabolism.

01:35:31.560 --> 01:35:35.820
I believe obesity is a
disease of brain circuits.

01:35:35.820 --> 01:35:37.230
- [Andrew] I do as well.

01:35:37.230 --> 01:35:41.145
- And so this view that we have,

01:35:41.145 --> 01:35:45.183
been working on for the
longest time, because,

01:35:46.080 --> 01:35:48.540
the molecules that we're
dealing with are in the body,

01:35:48.540 --> 01:35:52.860
not in the head, led us to to view,

01:35:52.860 --> 01:35:56.580
of course this issues and
problems has been one of

01:35:56.580 --> 01:35:58.560
metabolism, physiology, and so forth.

01:35:58.560 --> 01:36:03.240
They remain to be the carriers
of the ultimate signal,

01:36:03.240 --> 01:36:07.800
but the brain ultimately appears
to be the conductor of this

01:36:07.800 --> 01:36:11.460
orchestra of physiology and metabolism.

01:36:11.460 --> 01:36:15.213
All right, now let's go to
the gut brain and sugar,

01:36:16.710 --> 01:36:17.700
maybe.

01:36:17.700 --> 01:36:19.743
- Please, please.

01:36:20.913 --> 01:36:22.020
No, I mean,

01:36:22.020 --> 01:36:27.020
the vagus nerve has in popular
culture has been kind of

01:36:28.950 --> 01:36:33.950
converted into this single
meaning of calming pathways,

01:36:34.020 --> 01:36:37.110
mostly because I actually
have to tip my hat

01:36:37.110 --> 01:36:39.210
to the yogic community was

01:36:39.210 --> 01:36:43.053
among the first to talk
about vagus on and on and on,

01:36:44.340 --> 01:36:46.143
there are calming pathways,

01:36:47.280 --> 01:36:49.880
so-called parasympathetic
pathways within the vagus.

01:36:51.287 --> 01:36:52.800
But I think that the more
we learn about the vagus,

01:36:52.800 --> 01:36:57.060
the more it seems like an entire
set of neural connections,

01:36:57.060 --> 01:36:58.530
as opposed to one nerve.

01:36:58.530 --> 01:37:00.180
I just wanted to just
mention that because I think

01:37:00.180 --> 01:37:01.260
a lot of people have heard

01:37:01.260 --> 01:37:03.360
about the vagus turns out experimentally

01:37:03.360 --> 01:37:04.560
in the laboratory,

01:37:04.560 --> 01:37:07.050
many neuroscientists
will stimulate the vagus

01:37:07.050 --> 01:37:11.220
to create states of alertness
and arousal when animals,

01:37:11.220 --> 01:37:13.950
or even people believe it
or not are close to dying

01:37:13.950 --> 01:37:15.660
or going into coma stimulation

01:37:15.660 --> 01:37:16.770
of the vagus is one of the ways

01:37:16.770 --> 01:37:19.620
to wake up the brain counter to the idea

01:37:19.620 --> 01:37:22.200
that it's just this I way
of calming oneself down.

01:37:22.200 --> 01:37:24.060
- And also of course, I mean,

01:37:24.060 --> 01:37:26.223
one has to be cautious they're in that.

01:37:27.664 --> 01:37:30.750
So the vagus nerve is made

01:37:30.750 --> 01:37:33.423
out of many thousands of fibers,

01:37:34.710 --> 01:37:38.190
individual fibers that
make this gigantic bundle.

01:37:38.190 --> 01:37:40.500
And it's likely as we're speaking,

01:37:40.500 --> 01:37:42.880
that each of these fibers carries

01:37:43.837 --> 01:37:45.510
a slightly different meaning,

01:37:45.510 --> 01:37:48.840
not necessarily one by
one, maybe five is 10,

01:37:48.840 --> 01:37:50.373
five is 20, do all right,

01:37:51.393 --> 01:37:55.020
but they carry meaning that's associated

01:37:55.020 --> 01:37:58.140
with their specific task.

01:37:58.140 --> 01:38:00.810
This group of fibers is telling the brain

01:38:00.810 --> 01:38:02.913
about the state of your heart.

01:38:03.780 --> 01:38:05.400
This group of fiber is telling

01:38:05.400 --> 01:38:08.880
the brain about the state of your gut.

01:38:08.880 --> 01:38:13.050
This is telling your brain
about its nutritional state,

01:38:13.050 --> 01:38:17.430
this, your pancreas, this your lungs.

01:38:17.430 --> 01:38:22.430
And they are again, to make
the same simple example,

01:38:23.457 --> 01:38:25.713
the keys of this piano.

01:38:26.555 --> 01:38:28.260
Yes, you're right.

01:38:28.260 --> 01:38:30.483
There is a lot of data,

01:38:33.060 --> 01:38:37.867
showing that activating the
entire vagal bundle has very

01:38:39.390 --> 01:38:42.900
meaningful effects in a
wide range of conditions.

01:38:42.900 --> 01:38:47.900
In fact, it's being used to
treat untractable depression.

01:38:49.020 --> 01:38:50.223
- A little stimulator.

01:38:51.540 --> 01:38:53.253
- Epileptics seizures.

01:38:55.020 --> 01:38:57.030
But again, there are thousands

01:38:57.030 --> 01:38:59.580
of fibers carrying different functions.

01:38:59.580 --> 01:39:03.430
So to some degree this is like

01:39:06.720 --> 01:39:11.720
turning the lights on the stadium,

01:39:12.570 --> 01:39:15.150
